- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** Setting a recorded experiment's role, session and notes as semantic messages that write its file (001 §P `SetExperimentRole`; 001 §E 'notes on experiments … live in their files, so a reviewer's comments come back in the returned folder'; 001 §K role and session). The bay's controls that send them are step 296's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `Experiment`: `type Experiment with` `member this.withRole (role : ExperimentRole) : Experiment`, `member this.withSessionOpt (sessionOpt : SessionName option) : Experiment` and `member this.withNotes (notes : ExperimentNotes) : Experiment`, each the experiment with that field; and on `ExperimentCollection` `member this.withStoredExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : ExperimentCollection`, the collection with its experiment of that id replaced, unchanged when it holds none, the draft untouched. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SetExperimentRole of Experiments.ExperimentId * Experiments.ExperimentRole`, `SetExperimentSession of Experiments.ExperimentId * ControlCaption` (the typed text; a blank text clears the session) and `SetExperimentNotes of Experiments.ExperimentId * ControlCaption`, each with a one-line doc. Each arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. Otherwise, for the collection's experiment of that id (none: the model is unchanged and nothing is written), the changed experiment (`withRole`; `withSessionOpt (SessionName.tryCreate text.value)`; `withNotes (ExperimentNotes text.value)`) is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261 (7)(b)); on success the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`), and a failure keeps the model with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. An experiment's role, session and notes change nothing else: its scan, setup, name and data stay. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with E1 committed: `SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession and SetExperimentNotes change the stored experiment and its kit file`: `SetExperimentRole (E1, CalibrationRun)`, `SetExperimentSession (E1, ControlCaption "Day 1")` and `SetExperimentNotes (E1, ControlCaption "LR re-seated before this run")` leave the collection's E1 with that role, `Some (SessionName "Day 1")` and those notes, its scan unchanged, and `E1.experiment-json` read back through `readExperiments` holds the same three. `a blank session clears it, and a change to an experiment the kit lacks writes nothing`: then `SetExperimentSession (E1, ControlCaption "  ")` gives `sessionOpt = None` in the model and the file; `SetExperimentRole (ExperimentId 9, DarkRun)` leaves the model equal and every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 278): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends the three messages, with the same assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the bookkeeping messages land, `SetExperimentRole`, `SetExperimentSession` and `SetExperimentNotes` MUST change the stored experiment's role, session (a blank text clearing it) and notes and write its kit file, refused under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession and SetExperimentNotes change the stored experiment and its kit file` and `a blank session clears it, and a change to an experiment the kit lacks writes nothing`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
